Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840 size patch to fs/p9c.ad.
Applied by scripts/mkroot.sh in build/feather-nrf52840/root only; the
committed file is unchanged.

Reason: the nRF52840 has 256 KiB of RAM for everything: kernel data, kernel
stacks and heap, the files in / and every running program's stack and data
(boards/feather_nrf52840/link.ld; programs' code stays in flash).

    the message buffer of one 9P connection (kernel heap, while
    a server is mounted)   4120 bytes -> 1048 bytes
A read or write through a mount then moves at most 1024 bytes per request
(the client splits longer ones); the size is negotiated with the server at
mount time, so nothing else changes.

Only constants, array lengths, and messages that quote them change.
Generated by editing a copy and
    diff -u --label a/fs/p9c.ad --label b/fs/p9c.ad fs/p9c.ad <copy>

--- a/fs/p9c.ad
+++ b/fs/p9c.ad
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
 from mm.slab import kmalloc, kfree
 
 P9C_MAX: uint32 = 4                 # = the dimension of p9_conns
-P9C_MSIZE: uint32 = 4120            # one message: 4096 bytes of data and the largest header (a board may patch it)
+P9C_MSIZE: uint32 = 1048            # Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840: was 4120 (1024 bytes of data and the largest header)
 P9C_IOHDR: uint32 = 24
 P9C_PIPES: uint32 = 1
 P9C_DEVICE: uint32 = 2
